Not really.  Knowing you have the spell available on the ascension run 
(or for that matter, available when you want it) is much more important 
than having it for 40000 turns instead of 30000.  There are several 
spells that you don't want to expire in critical situations (cure 
sickness, magic missile come to mind, in slashem haste self, if you can 
protect yourself against pool spells only via water walking boots), but 
that you do not need for the whole length of the game.  So a valid 
strategy would be to let them expire for some time in the middle game, 
relearn and keep them by relearning in the end game.

